+# Feature Specification: Cancel Booking
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Implemented (open questions settled by assumption; no answer was available)
+**Input**: Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service: it cancels the booking at time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled once.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, `refund` in euro cents.
+- **FR-002**: A cancelled booking no longer clashes with other bookings and no longer hides the item from `availability`.
+- **FR-003**: Cancelling an already cancelled booking is an error; cancelling an unknown booking is an error.
+- **FR-004**: `at` is an ISO-8601 UTC instant (validated explicitly; no dependence on the machine clock).
+
+## Clarifications (assumed; no user input was available, change here if the school's policy differs)
+- **Refund rule** (`REFUND_*` constants in `src/index.ts`): `at` 24 hours or more before the booking start: full refund (the total). Less than 24 hours before the start: 50% of the total, rounded to the nearest cent, halves up. At or after the start: no refund (0).
+- **`at`** must be an ISO-8601 UTC time on the hour, like booking times. It may be after the start or end (refund 0); it is not checked against the booking's creation.
+- A cancelled booking keeps its id; cancelling it again throws.
+
+## Plan / Tasks
+- Add `cancelled` flag to stored bookings; clash and `availability` checks skip cancelled ones.
+- Add `cancel` to `RentalService`; add tests in `test/rental.test.ts`.
